From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Subject: command-not-found: fill the messages upstream has not translated

command-not-found 23.04.0's catalogs leave messages it prints untranslated in
three of the edition's nine languages: ten in Brazilian Portuguese and in
Traditional Chinese (its main header among them, "Command '%(command)s' not
found, but can be installed with:") and three in Japanese, so a person reads
English between translated lines. Polish, French, German, Korean and
Simplified Chinese are complete. Placeholders keep upstream's order.
The translations are by Claude for Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack), pt_BR for
Daniel's review; they are an offer for upstream's translators on Launchpad.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
